---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import V from '../components/V.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Lesson terms | Route 66 Driving School" description="Booking, payment and cancellation terms for Route 66 Driving School lessons.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Lesson terms</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 3 October 2026. These terms apply to all lessons and test-day bookings with {business.name}.</p>

      <h2>Before your first lesson</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must be 17 or over and hold a valid provisional (or full) driving licence.</li>
        <li>Please show us your licence at the first lesson.</li>
        <li>You must meet the eyesight standard: be able to read a number plate from 20 metres, with glasses or lenses if you need them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Lessons and payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lessons are two hours long unless we agree otherwise.</li>
        <li>Lessons are paid for in advance. Block bookings are paid when booked.</li>
        <li>The price we quote is the full price. There are no hidden extras.</li>
        <li>Lesson time starts and ends at the agreed pick-up point.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cancelling or moving a lesson</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give us at least 48 hours notice and we will move your lesson or refund it in full.</li>
        <li>Lessons cancelled with less than 48 hours notice, or missed, are normally charged in full.</li>
        <li>
          If we have to cancel, we will give you as much notice as we can and offer another time or a full refund. If we
          cancel with less than 48 hours notice, your next lesson is free of charge for the same length.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Block bookings and refunds</h2>
      <p>Unused hours from a block booking are refunded at the standard hourly rate, minus the discount already given.</p>

      <h2>Driving tests in our car</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You book and pay DVSA for your test. Please tell us your test date and time before booking so we can confirm the car is free.</li>
        <li>
          We may decline to take you to test if we believe you are not yet safe to pass, or if the car is unfit due to
          circumstances outside our control. If we decline, we will explain why.
        </li>
        <li>
          If your test is cancelled by DVSA, any refund for the test fee comes from DVSA. Our test-day charge will be
          moved to your new date.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Safety and conduct</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We will not give a lesson if we believe you are under the influence of alcohol or drugs. The lesson will be charged.</li>
        <li>Lessons are given in dual-control cars insured for driving tuition.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If something is not right, please tell us first and we will try to sort it out: <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}
          ><V v={business.email} /></a
        >. If you are still not happy, you can contact Citizens Advice, or report concerns about an instructor's conduct to
        DVSA at <a href="mailto:instructorconduct@dvsa.gov.uk">instructorconduct@dvsa.gov.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
